{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), which gives a weak RNA-only baseline and tells us nothing about whether the image modality carries useful signal. This is a multimodal cellular profiling study, so the single most consequential design question is whether the image branch contributes any predictive value at all. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides a clean unimodal image baseline using a standard, well-established backbone, directly comparable in structure to config_001. Why it is the best next experiment: (1) If image accuracy is substantially higher than 0.485, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies investing subsequent experiments in fusion strategies; if it is similarly low, it suggests the image modality may not be informative and we should focus budget on RNA encoder and profile improvements. (2) It partitions the remaining 50 untested configs into two strategic branches (image-useful vs. image-not-useful), dramatically reducing search-space uncertainty with a single run. (3) resnet50 is a reasonable, fast-to-train first probe before committing to the heavier ViT-L variants. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about the overall architecture under the limited budget."
}

